<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee co-op stocks 3.87 mln bags in August.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee co-op stocks 3.87 mln bags in August.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coffee stocks held by Brazilian co-operatives totaled 3.87 million 60.5 kg bags August 31, National Coffee Council (CNC) said in a statement.</p>
<p>This is up from the 2.63 million bags held by co-ops as of July. It is also higher than the 3.27 million bags held at the same period last year, it added.</p>
<p>Co-ops received 2.02 million bags of coffee during August which is 107.5 percent higher than the 974,040 bags delivered in August 1995, but it is down from the 2.13 million bags received in the same month 1994.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 232 4411.</p>
